# `[a, b] = [b, a + b]` makes no array. The old b becomes the new a and the sum becomes the new b at the back edge: one addition, the poll, the counter.
# CHECK-LABEL: steps by 1
# CHECK: Double b@[[a]] = Phi(
# CHECK-NEXT: Double b@[[b]] = Phi(
# CHECK: Double b@[[sum]] = Add(b@[[a]], b@[[b]], {{*}}:Add)
# CHECK-NEXT: Patchpoint({{*}}isLoopPoll{{*}}:LoopHint)
# CHECK-NOT: Patchpoint
# CHECK-NOT: Reads:
# CHECK-NOT: Writes:
# CHECK: Upsilon(b@[[b]], ^[[a]], WritesLocalState
# CHECK-NEXT: Upsilon(b@[[sum]], ^[[b]], WritesLocalState
# CHECK-NOT: Patchpoint
# CHECK-LABEL: end of loop
# X64: loop #{{*}}, instructions: 6, patchpoints: 1, {{*}} steps by 1
# ARM64: loop #{{*}}, instructions: 6, patchpoints: 1, {{*}} steps by 1
